i) Rewrite the following `if-else-if` code snippet into an equivalent `switch` statement in Java:
```java
int code = 2;
if (code == 1) {
    System.out.println("Silver Member");
} else if (code == 2) {
    System.out.println("Gold Member");
} else if (code == 3) {
    System.out.println("Platinum Member");
} else {
    System.out.println("Standard Guest");
}
```

questions.answer:
**Equivalent Java `switch` statement:**
```java
int code = 2;
switch (code) {
    case 1:
        System.out.println("Silver Member");
        break;
    case 2:
        System.out.println("Gold Member");
        break;
    case 3:
        System.out.println("Platinum Member");
        break;
    default:
        System.out.println("Standard Guest");
        break;
}
```

