ii) Convert the following entry-controlled `for` loop into an exit-controlled `do-while` loop in Java:
```java
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 5; i <= 25; i += 5) {
    sum += i;
}
System.out.println("Sum = " + sum);
```

questions.answer:
**Equivalent `do-while` loop:**
```java
int sum = 0;
int i = 5;
do {
    sum += i;
    i += 5;
} while (i <= 25);
System.out.println("Sum = " + sum);
```

**Output:** `Sum = 75` (5 + 10 + 15 + 20 + 25 = 75).

